# Bank Churn Prediction Model

## Overview

This project builds a predictive machine learning pipeline using XGBoost to identify bank customers at high risk of churning (Exited = 1). 

By analyzing customer demographics, account details, and engagement behaviors, the model enables proactive customer retention strategies.

## Key Findings & EDA 

InsightsAge: Older customers exhibit significantly higher churn rates compared to younger demographics.

Engagement: Disengaged customers (IsActiveMember = 0) represent the majority of exits.

Credit Score: Customers in the low credit band <400 experienced a 100% churn rate.

Geography: Customers residing in Germany showed the highest proportion of churn compared to France and Spain.

## Workflow & Methodology

Data Preprocessing & Feature Engineering:
One-Hot Encoded categorical variables (Gender, Geography, and created CreditBand).
Scaled numerical features using StandardScaler.
Handling Class Imbalance:Applied scale_pos_weight (~3.09 to 3.86) to address the ~4:1 ratio between retained and churned customers.

Model Optimization:
Tuned hyperparameters using RandomizedSearchCV targeting ROC-AUC and F1-Score.
Model explainability analyzed using SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) values.

## Performance Metrics

Accuracy: ~83.75%

ROC-AUC Score: ~86.50%

Churn (Class 1) Recall: 72%

Churn (Class 1) Precision: 57%

Churn (Class 1) F1-Score: 0.63
